WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.859
Welcome to the Tueri Systems Risk Brief for Saturday, October thirty-first.

2
00:00:04.859 --> 00:00:07.792
Operational clarity when conditions change.

3
00:00:07.792 --> 00:00:12.519
A few minutes on what is happening, what can be confirmed, and what has changed.

4
00:00:12.519 --> 00:00:14.066
Digitally narrated.

5
00:00:14.066 --> 00:00:20.876
A ship was attacked inside the Arabian Gulf on Friday, and an earlier Hormuz attack has only now been reported.

6
00:00:20.876 --> 00:00:25.509
The US Embassy in Honduras flagged a threat near Puerto Cortés this weekend.

7
00:00:25.509 --> 00:00:28.411
A Philippine volcano is at alert level three.

8
00:00:28.411 --> 00:00:32.450
And Britain has updated its advice on the Ethiopia and Kenya border.

9
00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:34.939
Here's the detail.

10
00:00:34.939 --> 00:00:37.913
Shipping first.

11
00:00:37.913 --> 00:00:50.278
Confirmed by UK Maritime Trade Operations: on Friday evening local time, a vessel about forty nautical miles off Iran's coast, inside the Arabian Gulf and well west of the Strait of Hormuz, was hit on the port side by an unknown projectile.

12
00:00:50.278 --> 00:00:52.689
It caught fire; the crew is safe.

13
00:00:52.689 --> 00:01:02.917
A verified report published Friday adds a crude tanker struck while leaving the strait on Wednesday, reported two days after it occurred, so the known incident record has grown.

14
00:01:02.917 --> 00:01:10.446
Reported: Oman's maritime security center says it evacuated twenty-five crew from a burning tanker in the strait on Friday.

15
00:01:10.446 --> 00:01:19.345
Claim only: Iran's Revolutionary Guard navy says four tankers on what it calls unauthorized routes were stopped, some after hitting mines.

16
00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:23.135
Reported: US Central Command denies the mine claims.

17
00:01:23.135 --> 00:01:26.192
It is not clear whether any of these are the same ships.

18
00:01:26.192 --> 00:01:35.989
The Joint Maritime Information Center rates the threat as severe in the Strait of Hormuz and substantial in the wider Arabian Gulf, where Friday's projectile attack fell.

19
00:01:35.989 --> 00:01:44.460
Tueri suggests operators in the Gulf, not only in the strait, review hull watch and routing with their security providers.

20
00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:45.073
Honduras.

21
00:01:45.073 --> 00:01:55.240
The US Embassy issued a security alert about a reported threat to bridges and access routes around Puerto Cortés early Saturday and advised avoiding the area this weekend.

22
00:01:55.240 --> 00:02:01.285
Reported: Honduras' security minister said there is no evidence of a credible plot and it may be a false alarm.

23
00:02:01.285 --> 00:02:06.368
Port authorities raised the port's security level, and terminals are reported to be operating.

24
00:02:06.368 --> 00:02:14.094
Tueri suggests confirming routes with freight agents before moving cargo or staff there this weekend.

25
00:02:14.094 --> 00:02:16.164
Philippines.

26
00:02:16.164 --> 00:02:26.747
Reported, via the US Embassy and media: the national volcano institute raised Mayon volcano to alert level three after an explosive eruption on Friday and recommends evacuation of the six kilometer danger zone.

27
00:02:26.747 --> 00:02:31.302
We found no reported airline cancellations.

28
00:02:31.302 --> 00:02:34.485
Ethiopia and Kenya.

29
00:02:34.485 --> 00:02:43.716
Confirmed by British travel advice updated Friday: violence in the Ethiopian border town of Moyale has affected the border area, with stray gunfire reported on the Kenyan side and disruption at the crossing.

30
00:02:43.716 --> 00:02:51.574
Britain advises vehicles crossing at Moyale to stay on the main A2 road and drive on to the next major town before stopping.

31
00:02:51.574 --> 00:03:04.137
Its Ethiopia advice, also updated, says avoid all travel within ten kilometers of the Kenyan border, except the Moyale road and town, where it advises against all but essential travel.

32
00:03:04.137 --> 00:03:06.406
Guyana.

33
00:03:06.406 --> 00:03:16.276
Confirmed by Georgia Tech measurements: internet traffic dropped sharply Friday morning when a transmission line failure cut power across Demerara and Berbice, and recovered by midday Central.

34
00:03:16.276 --> 00:03:27.726
Reported: the utility says about ninety percent of affected customers were reconnected, and it suspects deliberate interference, without naming anyone or giving evidence.

35
00:03:27.726 --> 00:03:30.392
Operations check.

36
00:03:30.392 --> 00:03:41.430
Aviation: at about one thirty-five p.m. local time, Flightradar twenty-four showed about three percent of Dammam flights cancelled, against ten percent at the same time Friday, on similar schedules.

37
00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:45.784
Riyadh showed about nineteen percent cancelled, on a smaller schedule.

38
00:03:45.784 --> 00:03:46.678
These are single snapshots, not a trend.

39
00:03:46.678 --> 00:03:53.974
Reported: the Saudi-led coalition says it downed a Houthi drone over Medina on Friday; the Houthis deny it.

40
00:03:53.974 --> 00:04:02.357
Maritime, claim only: Iran's Hormuz authority says action against vessels of a South Korean shipping group starts Sunday, without saying what action.

41
00:04:02.357 --> 00:04:09.714
Ports, reported: Friday's dockworker strikes blocked port access in Genoa and tied up ferries in Piraeus.

42
00:04:09.714 --> 00:04:14.242
Borders and health: no change to the US Ebola attestation rule, which applies to flights from eleven fifty-nine p.m.

43
00:04:14.242 --> 00:04:18.508
Eastern on Tuesday.

44
00:04:18.508 --> 00:04:27.467
Infrastructure, reported: Sudan's state electricity company says drone attacks on power stations have left Omdurman short of power and water.

45
00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:36.607
Ground transport: the Madrid to Andalusia high-speed line is still closed; Spanish media cite unnamed sources pointing to November fourteenth, not yet confirmed.

46
00:04:36.607 --> 00:04:38.106
That's today's brief.

47
00:04:38.106 --> 00:04:39.610
Current as of five forty-five a.m.

48
00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:43.173
Central, Saturday.

49
00:04:43.173 --> 00:04:45.594
Tueri summarizes public reporting.

50
00:04:45.594 --> 00:04:50.190
It is not legal, medical, or security advice for any specific situation.

51
00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:52.683
Check the original source before you act.

52
00:04:52.683 --> 00:05:01.846
Tueri Systems provides information verification, communications support, and operational decision support for organizations working in changing conditions.

53
00:05:01.846 --> 00:05:04.632
Learn more at tuerisystems.com.

54
00:05:04.632 --> 00:05:05.766
Thanks for listening.
